# Cellix structure

New application code follows the Cellix file roles. Data and behavior may differ. Structure may not.

- Domain: `*.aggregate.ts`, `*.entity.ts`, `*.value-objects.ts`, `*.repository.ts` (interface), `*.uow.ts` (interface), visa, passport, permissions, `*.event.ts`
- Application services: `contexts/<context>/<kebab-action>.ts` exports `export const <camelAction> = (dataSources: DataSources, ...ports) => async (command) => result`
- `create` / `update` / `delete` call `withScopedTransaction`. `query` / `get` / `find` use `readonlyDataSource`
- Persistence: `datasources/domain/<context>/<entity>/*.(repository|domain-adapter|uow).ts` implements the domain contract
- Models: `models/<entity>/<entity>.model.ts` exports `<Pascal>ModelFactory`, `<Pascal>ModelType`, `<Pascal>ModelName`. `models/<entity>/<entity>.seed.ts` exports `<camel>Seed`, one example document. Insert it into the database
- REST and GraphQL call `applicationServices` only. A REST handler calls `applicationServices.<Context>.<Entity>.<action>(command)`. It does not keep an array of documents. Resolvers are `*.resolvers.ts` files with a default `Resolvers` export

Do not add helper, util, common, or shared modules in these packages. Generate a new context, entity, or action with `@cellix/generator`. A change to data or behavior in a structure that already exists does not need the generator. Course catalog search and enrollment are examples of new structures, not the only work allowed. The files the generator writes are a scaffold. It prints the files to edit. The barrels are already wired. Do not copy `<camel>Seed` into a handler or a read repository. While editing, run `pnpm run agent-check -- pnpm run check`. The last check is `pnpm run agent-check -- pnpm run verify`. Do not glob a whole tree or read `node_modules` or `packages/cellix`.